This repository is a throughline *source*: a requirements graph, not a program. Its
items are Time Back Solutions' own plain-language rules, expressed as a grounded IDD
graph so consuming projects can compose it with throughline-compose.

The rules are informed by the international consensus on plain language — principally
ISO 24495-1:2023 (Plain language, Part 1: Governing principles and guidelines) and the
International Plain Language Federation's definition. Those standards are referenced,
not reproduced: each item's attrs.source_ref points at the governing principle it
elaborates, and no ISO text is copied here. ISO 24495-1:2023 is available from ISO.
